CORS stands for Cross-Origin Resource Sharing.
It’s a browser security feature that controls how a web page can make requests to a server that’s on a different origin 


# config/db.js

This file connects to MongoDB using Mongoose.

It takes the MongoDB URL from .env.

It establishes the database connection.

It is imported inside server.js.

# controllers folder

Controllers handle the logic for each route.

**chatController.js

Receives the user’s chat request.

Extracts user message.

Calls aiService.js to get a meal plan response from AI.

Saves the conversation message (optional).

Returns the AI response to the front-end.

This is where AI → DB → Response happens.

mealPlanController.js

Handles requests related to stored meal plans.

Example tasks:

Save a meal plan to DB

Fetch all meal plans

Fetch a specific one

Delete one

Think of it as “Meal Plan Manager”.

models folder

These define how data is structured in MongoDB.

ChatMessage.js

Schema for storing chat messages.

Each message has: role ("user" or "ai"), text, timestamp.

Optional if you want a chat history.

MealPlan.js

Schema for storing the meal plans returned by AI.

It holds:

title

dailyCalories

goals (weight loss / gain / etc.)

meals (array of meals per day)

createdAt (timestamp)

This structure matches exactly what we tell the AI to return.

routes folder

Routes define the URLs/endpoints your frontend or Postman calls.

chatRoutes.js

Defines routes like POST /api/chat

Sends requests to chatController.js.

Example:

router.post("/chat", chatController.handleChat);

mealPlanRoutes.js

Defines routes for meal plans

GET /api/meal-plans

POST /api/meal-plans

Sends requests to mealPlanController.js.

services folder

This folder is for logic that is not tied to routing or database.

aiService.js

Calls the AI API (OpenAI, Gemini, etc.)

Sends structured prompts.

Forces the AI to return clean JSON, not messy text.

Returns the result to chatController.js.

This file prevents AI chaos. It is the brain of the AI communication.

server.js

This is the entry point.

Imports express, sets up middleware (like JSON parsing).

Connects to MongoDB using db.js.

Loads the routes (chatRoutes, mealPlanRoutes).

Starts the server (app.listen).

Basically:
This file wakes up your backend.

.env

Stores sensitive keys: